[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798190103","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3798190103","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3798190103,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iY8gX","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T07:16:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T07:16:49Z","body":"Looks expected. As far as I know, exported variables are initialized **after** `_enter_tree()` callback, so this line `vbox.add_child(instance)` will lead to crash.\nSee https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/5492","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798190103/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798496801","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3798496801","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3798496801,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iaHYh","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T08:53:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T08:54:43Z","body":"Even if you put the `@onready` initialization aside and fetch the node inline in `_enter_tree`, the script still fails. It's because the array is never cleared during `_exit_tree`, which eventually leads to `queue_free` being called again on already-nulled instances from the prior frame.\n\nMy point here is that regardless of how things are initialized or managed in the script (e.g., an array not being cleared), the script should under no circumstances cause the editor to crash. If nothing else, the GDScript VM should report an error when that code path runs under `DEBUG_ENABLED` and the `base_obj` instance is `null`, and silently does nothing on non-debug builds (although I'd argue maybe this corner case it should continue to report an error).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798496801/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798882761","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3798882761","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3798882761,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iblnJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T10:28:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T10:28:51Z","body":"I'd say this is potentially unavoidable and part of the disclaimer that running code in `@tool` is unsafe and has risky cases, in fact the documentation [mentions this](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/plugins/running_code_in_the_editor.html#what-is-tool) involving `queue_free`","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798882761/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798896935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3798896935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3798896935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ibpEn","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T10:32:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T10:35:01Z","body":"Yes, but the fact that this is a `@tool` script is mostly irrelevant; it's just an easy way to manifest the crash. \n\nIf a non-tool script cached a set of non-refcounted objects in an array and mistakenly called queue_free or free on a no-longer-valid `base_obj`, the same crash would happen, just instead of the editor, the game would crash.\n\nI'm just asking GDScript to guard against this at the VM level with a meaningful error that outlines where the error originates, given that trying to backtrace this can be very difficult to isolate the offending script line.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798896935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799052808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3799052808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3799052808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7icPII","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T11:14:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T11:14:44Z","body":"Ok, I tested \"MRP\" and got zero crashes. Only errors in console.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799052808/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799093324","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3799093324","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3799093324,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7icZBM","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T11:26:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T11:26:19Z","body":"There should be an error like: \"instance is null\"","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799093324/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799121557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3799121557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3799121557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7icf6V","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T11:34:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T11:34:40Z","body":"> Ok, I tested \"MRP\" and got zero crashes. Only errors in console.\n\nOn which Godot version, because I tested 4.6.rc2 and 4.5.1 on Linux, both crash.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799121557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799385697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3799385697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3799385697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7idgZh","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T12:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T12:34:41Z","body":"> 4.6.rc2 and 4.5.1 on Linux, both crash.\n\nBoth, on Windows.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3799385697/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801962332","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3801962332","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3801962332,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7inVdc","user":{"login":"RoyBerube","id":30374490,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzc0NDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30374490?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube","html_url":"https://github.com/RoyBerube","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RoyBerube/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T22:01:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T22:01:03Z","body":"Note for anyone looking into this and is unfamiliar with the run order: @onready happens after _enter_tree(). The problem is a null pointer for vbox in _enter_tree(). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3801962332/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816895557","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3816895557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3816895557,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jgTRF","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T10:49:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T12:07:59Z","body":"On linux\n\nNull value with `@onready` is just a noise that doesn't actually add anything and is not relevant.\n\n<img width=\"1913\" height=\"1054\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6984d7da-a95a-4eac-8ab3-c7b3d65d33e7\" />\n\nAs mentioned, the actual problem is forgetting to call `border_element_array.clear()` in `_exit_tree` after you `queue_free` nodes. `_enter_tree` and `_exit_tree` will run on the same instance when you switch tabs, so it will lead to calling `queue_free` on already freed object after a couple of switches.\n\nAfter testing calling any method on freed object causes crash, so the minimum reproduction is basically\n```swift\nfunc _enter_tree() -> void:\n    print(\"hello world\")\n    var instance = TextureRect.new()\n    instance.free()\n    instance.print_tree()\n```\nAlso null instances and freed instances are really 2 different things, despite gdscript claiming that `freed_instance == null` is true.\n\nI figure this is mainly a problem for tool scripts as running project correctly shows error `Attempt to call function 'print_tree' in base 'previously freed' on a null instance.` in debugger. Also this is what gets printed on actual `null` value `Invalid call. Nonexistent function 'print_tree' in base 'Nil'.` which was achieved with\n```swift\nfunc _enter_tree() -> void:\n    print(\"hello world\")\n    var instance = TextureRect.new()\n    instance.free()\n    instance = null\n    instance.print_tree()\n```\nHuh, typed instance (`instance: TextureRect`) prints `Cannot call method 'print_tree' on a previously freed instance.` and `Cannot call method 'print_tree' on a null value.`. Also it doesn't crash in editor now... another win for the static types? Typed array also doesn't crash. ~~I guess only `Variant` type forgets to check it before call?~~ Type `Object` also crashes editor, so looks like only validated calls get checked for freed instance.\n\nSo to sum this, this only really affects tool editor scripts when you call function on freed instance and gdscript can't statically verify function call. Also setting properties on freed objects doesn't crash editor, so this only affects function calls","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816895557/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816970121","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-3816970121","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":3816970121,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jgleJ","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T11:07:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T11:07:29Z","body":"That's correct @NoctemCat, thank you for the careful review & analysis, confirming what I thought I was seeing 🙏 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816970121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4107196189","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115375#issuecomment-4107196189","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115375","id":4107196189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc70ztcd","user":{"login":"ssaenger","id":28540972,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NTQwOTcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28540972?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger","html_url":"https://github.com/ssaenger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ssaenger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-22T23:25:05Z","updated_at":"2026-03-22T23:34:23Z","body":"I've run into this issue today, calling `free()` twice on an already freed object. But setting that object to `null` between the free calls avoids the crash.\n\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends Node2D\n\nvar obj = load(\"res://a_script.gd\")\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tobj = obj.new()\n\tprint(obj)\n\t# Do something with children nodes...\n\n\nfunc _exit_tree() -> void:\n\tobj.free()\n\t# Uncomment following line avoids the crash\n\t#obj = null\n\tprint(obj)\n```\nIn the editor, this script is attached to a node that is the scene root. There's another, irrelevant scene opened too. Swap scenes and the crash occurs because `_exit_tree()` was called twice. The editor doesn't unload/load scenes when tabbing to a different scene, so I guess that makes sense.\n\nI feel like this is an easy trap to fall into because most of the time you would override `_ready()` to run initialization code since your children are ready at that point. There isn't an `_unready()` function to deinitialize (i.e. free objects), so it seems like `_exit_tree()` is the place to do it. I had the false sense of security that `_ready()` is always run before `_exit_tree()` but obviously that isn't true and I didn't know how the editor manages scenes until now.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4107196189/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]